---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import NodeGraph from "../components/NodeGraph.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Contact"
  description="Get in touch with SemanticKC about a website build for your local service business."
>
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden px-4 py-20 text-center sm:px-6 sm:py-24 lg:px-8">
    <NodeGraph compact />
    <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-2xl">
      <p class="font-display mb-4 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-accent-300">Contact</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-5xl">
        Let's Talk About Your Site
      </h1>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg text-white/65">
        Send a short note about your business and what you're looking for — we'll follow up to set
        up a discovery conversation.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="px-4 pb-16 sm:px-6 sm:pb-24 lg:px-8">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
      <div class="min-w-0 rounded-3xl border border-line bg-card px-6 py-10 text-center sm:px-10 sm:py-12">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">Email Us</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-white/65">
          The fastest way to reach us is email. Include a bit about your business and what you're
          hoping the site will do for you.
        </p>
        <a
          href="mailto:admin@semantickc.com?subject=New%20project%20inquiry"
          class="mt-6 inline-flex max-w-full items-center justify-center break-words rounded-full bg-accent-500 px-8 py-3.5 text-base font-bold text-white transition-colors hover:bg-accent-600"
        >
          admin@semantickc.com
        </a>
        <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-white/50">Kansas City metro &middot; Response within 1–2 business days</p>
      </div>

      <!--
        DRAFT NOTE FOR SEAN (not shown to site visitors — this is an HTML
        comment): this is a static site with no backend, so a real
        server-side contact form isn't wired up here on purpose. A
        mailto: link is the simplest option and has zero third-party
        dependency, which is why it's the default below.

        If you'd rather visitors fill out an actual form (no email client
        popup), a lightweight service like Formspree or Web3Forms can
        receive a plain HTML form POST without any backend of our own —
        but that does add a third-party dependency this build otherwise
        avoids. Flagging it as an explicit option rather than silently
        adding it. Let me know if you want that instead and which service
        you'd prefer.
      -->
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
